I walk on the street.
But where is the sea?
There are only tall buildings around.
I do not understand the way.
I am on the wrong road.
There is a small shop ahead.
There is an elderly man in the shop.
I go towards the shop.
"Kaka, hello."
"Where is Marine Drive?" I ask.
"I do not see the sea."
Kaka smiles.
"Madam, this road is wrong," he says.
"You go straight from here."
"Turn right at the next corner."
"Then keep walking straight towards the sea."
"Marine Drive is there."
"Thank you Kaka," I say.
I turn right and walk straight.
